---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_362",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 362,
  "text": "[[1524.14]] <b>304.  Infiniti possunt gradus esse inter animas [1686 (?)]</b>\n [[1524.15]] <tab/>[1686 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[1524.22]] Infiniti possunt gradus esse inter animas, idque similitudine petita a nostra Geometria\n[[1524.23]] sublimiore videtur illustrari posse. Animae est connectere inter se differentes\n[[1524.24]] corporis status, ut ejus ope praeterita et futura simul existant, praeterita per quandam\n[[1525.1]] reminiscentiam, futura per praesensionem. Et licet verum sit corpus etiam praeteritos et\n[[1525.2]] praesentes suos status referre; hoc tamen interest, quod in corpore non est nisi praesens\n[[1525.3]] status, etsi is sit effectus praeteriti referens causam; et idem sit causa futuri referens\n[[1525.4]] effectum. Sed in anima omnis status per se repraesentatur, praeteritus ut praeteritus,\n[[1525.5]] futurus ut futurus, praesens ut praesens; unusquisque non solum exprimitur per consequentiam,\n[[1525.6]] sed et repraesentatur. </p>\n<p> [[1525.7]] Repraesentandi tamen modus plus minusve est clarus plenusque pro animae perfectione;\n[[1525.8]] ut transitus in lineis suos gradus habent. Nempe in omni linea curva transitus est\n[[1525.9]] a puncto ad punctum. Quod si jam linea concipiatur ut polygonum infinitorum laterum;\n[[1525.10]] utique pro transitu seu progressu in linea considerare oportet puncta plura. Nam unum\n[[1525.11]] punctum praesentem quidem statum designat, non tamen mutationem. Si conjungamus\n[[1525.12]] tantum duo puncta, exprimetur directio motus seu quae sit tangens lineae; si tria puncta\n[[1525.13]] conjungamus, habetur non tantum directio, sed et flexus, seu mutatio directionis; adeoque\n[[1525.14]] habetur circulus osculans. Si conjungamus puncta quatuor, habebitur osculum secundi\n[[1525.15]] gradus; et ita porro. Sed his omnibus nondum exprimitur plena lineae curvedo, quae\n[[1525.16]] omnia possibilia oscula simul involvit; exprimitque quaenam sit linea osculans cujuscunque\n[[1525.17]] gradus. Corpus respondet situi puncti seu statui praesenti; sed animae respondent\n[[1525.18]] gradui mutationis in motu puncti. Et Anima infimi gradus respondet directioni, anima\n[[1525.19]] secundi gradus osculo primo, anima tertii gradus osculo secundo; et ita porro. Sed mens\n[[1525.20]] respondet osculo infiniti gradus; et exprimit integram lineae curvedinem in puncto dato,\n[[1525.21]] seu quicquid a puncto dato non abest assignabiliter. Unde patet Mentes esse ad simplices\n[[1525.22]] animas ut infinitum ad finitum, seu ut finitum ad infinite parvum. Sed mens infinita\n[[1525.23]] respondet toti progressui motus per lineam, transitui a puncto dato ad aliud punctum\n[[1525.24]] assignabiliter distans quodcunque, seu saltum. </p>\n<p> [[1526.1]] Quod si quis putet distingui hic rursus posse inter Mentes saltum facientes per\n[[1526.2]] distantias finitas diversas, quae omnes Mentem saltu carentem infinite excedant; et tamen\n[[1526.3]] ipsae sint infinite depressae infra mentem cujus saltus est in distantias omnes, dicendum\n[[1526.4]] tamen ubi mera est continuitas seu sola differentia per majus et minus non posse diversas\n[[1526.5]] species assignari, adeoque mentem quae saltum faciat, facere in quantamcumque distantiam\n[[1526.6]] cum [oscula] numeris seu discreto differre sit manifestum.\n [[1526.7]] <petit> </p>\n<p> [[1526.8]] <i>Nach den beiden verworfenen Ansätzen in Kleindruck hat Leibniz das nachfolgende Schema entwickelt</i>:\n[[1526.9]] <tab/>Habemus ergo\n [[1526.10]] <picture>8054</picture>\n [[1526.11]] Punctum seu statum <tab/>Progressum\n [[1526.12]] <tab/><picture>8048</picture>\n [[1526.13]] <tab/>directionem <tab/>flexum\n[[1526.14]] <tab/>Habemus ergo\n [[1526.15]] <picture>8083</picture>\n [[1526.16]] Punctum seu statum <tab/>Progressum\n [[1526.17]] <tab/><picture>8064</picture>\n [[1526.18]] <tab/>elementarem <tab/>plenum\n [[1526.19]] <tab/><picture>8050</picture>\n [[1526.20]] <tab/>directionem <tab/>flexum\n [[1526.21]] <tab/>tangentis <tab/>osculantis\n [[1526.22]] <tab/>pro gradu\n [[1526.23]] <tab/><picture>8048</picture>\n [[1526.24]] <tab/>primo, <tab/>secundo, <tab/>tertio etc. </petit>\n [[1527.1]] <tab/>Habemus ergo\n [[1527.2]] <picture>8106</picture>\n [[1527.3]] Punctum seu statum <tab/>Progressum\n [[1527.4]] <tab/><picture>8064</picture>\n [[1527.5]] <tab/>elementarem <tab/>absolutum\n [[1527.6]] <tab/>seu inchoatum\n [[1527.7]] <tab/><picture>8076</picture>\n [[1527.8]] <tab/>partialem <tab/>totalem lineae\n [[1527.9]] <tab/>secundum <tab/>speciem exprimentem\n [[1527.10]] <picture>8074</picture>\n [[1527.11]] directionem tangentis <tab/>flexum <tab/>osculi\n [[1527.12]] <tab/>in gradu\n [[1527.13]] <tab/><picture>8050</picture>\n [[1527.14]] <tab/>primo, <tab/>secundo, <tab/>tertio etc.\n [[1527.15]] Status <tab/>Directio <tab/>Osculum <tab/>Lineatio <tab/>Linea\n [[1527.16]] <tab/>primi, <tab/>secundi, <tab/>tertii <tab/>utcunque\n [[1527.17]] <tab/>gradus<tab/>producta\n [[1527.19]] <tab/>Respondent his\n [[1527.21]] Corpus <tab/>Anima ima <tab/>sensus <tab/>Anima <tab/>Deus\n [[1527.22]] <tab/>seu vita <tab/>primi, <tab/>secundi, <tab/>tertii <tab/>intelligens\n [[1527.23]] <tab/>gradus\n [[1527.24]] <tab/><picture>9048</picture> <tab/>seu\n [[1527.25]] <tab/><picture>9064</picture>\n [[1527.26]] <tab/>rationis expers <tab/>rationalis\n [[1527.27]] <tab/><picture>9069</picture>\n [[1527.28]] <tab/>finitum. Anima <tab/>infinitum\n [[1527.29]] <tab/><picture>9064</picture>\n [[1527.30]] Aggregatum, quod per se torpet <tab/>una substantia, seu vivum\n [[1527.31]] <picture>9130</picture>\n [[1527.32]] <tab/>Substans </p>\n",
  "number": "304.",
  "title": "Infiniti possunt gradus esse inter animas",
  "date": "[1686 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:304. Infiniti possunt gradus esse inter animas [1686 (?)] [1686 (?)] Infiniti possunt gradus esse inter animas, idque similitudine petita a nostra Geometria sublimiore videtur illustrari posse. Animae est connectere inter se differentes corporis status, ut ejus ope praeterita et futura simul existan...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>